98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Modern enterprises rely on third-party SaaS integrations that use REST APIs and OAuth tokens to enable seamless data sharing and workflows. However, these integrations often have broad, static permissions, allowing access to more data than necessary. While organizations assume integrations only access permitted data, hidden API endpoints and over-permissioned tokens can expose sensitive information. The lack of automated mechanisms to verify actual runtime behavior makes security audits largely manual and incomplete, increasing the risk of unnoticed data access.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
